entry.summary:
I just open-sourced @mawtech/glass-ui — a React component library featuring that sleek Apple macOS/visionOS glassmorphism design. I built this because I was tired of recreating the same glass effects for every project. Blurred backgrounds, subtle borders, smooth animations, it takes forever to get right. So I packaged it all into a reusable library. And now it's free for everyone. 18 production-ready React components with: ✨ Apple-inspired glassmorphism design 🌙 Dark mode optimized 📝 Full TypeScript support 🎬 Framer Motion animations ♿ Accessible (WCAG 2.1 AA) 🌳 Tree-shakeable npm install @mawtech/glass-ui
Then import the styles: import '@mawtech/glass-ui/styles.css';
That's it. You're ready to go. The foundation of any glass UI: import { GlassCard } from '@mawtech/glass-ui';
